%% State machine of one statement: checked by code first, then by staff.
%% agents/tools.ts (record_statement) and server/routes/staff.ts (review).
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  [*] --> Checking : agent calls record_statement
  Checking --> Verified : every quote on its page,<br/>every number in a quote
  Checking --> RejectedByChecker : a check fails<br/>(statement.rejected, with reasons)
  RejectedByChecker --> [*] : the agent may fix it<br/>and call again
  Verified --> Approved : staff approve
  Verified --> Edited : staff edit the wording
  Verified --> RejectedByStaff : staff reject, with a note
  Edited --> Edited : citations re-checked by code,<br/>approval keeps it "edited"
  Approved --> Shown : brief published
  Edited --> Shown : brief published
  Shown --> [*]
  RejectedByStaff --> [*]

  Checking : Checking (code)
  Verified : Verified
  Verified : stored in the draft brief
  RejectedByChecker : Rejected by checker
  RejectedByChecker : never stored in a brief,<br/>only in the record
  Approved : Approved
  Edited : Edited
  Edited : original text kept,<br/>"Edited by staff" badge
  RejectedByStaff : Rejected by staff
  RejectedByStaff : left out of the published brief
  Shown : Shown to residents
  Shown : with its citations
  note left of Checking
    The checker runs again after every staff edit.
    If a quote no longer matches, the statement
    shows a "Not verified" badge to staff and residents.
  end note
